"host is present, so you don't necesita exclude it."

#: ../../getting_started/requirements/opensearch_configuration.rst:79
msgid ""
"In secure mode, ``admin_dn`` and ``nodes_dn`` default to "
"``O=Morpheus,OU=Ops,CN=<node_name>`` and are set automatically per node. "
"These only need to be overridden when using custom certificates (see "
"below)."
msgstr ""
"In secure mode, ``admin_dn`` y ``nodes_dn`` predeterminado to "
"``O=Morpheus,OU=Ops,CN=<node_name>`` y are set automatically per node. "
"These only necesita be overridden when using personalizado certificates "
"(see below)."

#: ../../getting_started/requirements/opensearch_configuration.rst:82
msgid "Custom Certificates (admin_dn and nodes_dn)"
msgstr "Custom Certificates (admin_dn y nodes_dn)"

#: ../../getting_started/requirements/opensearch_configuration.rst:84
msgid ""
"When using your own certificates instead of the auto-generated ones, set "
"``admin_dn`` and ``nodes_dn`` to match the subject DN of your "
"certificates. These values map to ``plugins.security.authcz.admin_dn`` "
"and ``plugins.security.nodes_dn`` in ``opensearch.yml``."
msgstr ""
"When using your own certificates instead of the auto-generated ones, set "
"``admin_dn`` y ``nodes_dn`` to match the subject DN of your certificates. "
"These values map to ``plugins.security.authcz.admin_dn`` y "
"``plugins.security.nodes_dn`` in ``opensearch.yml``."

#: ../../getting_started/requirements/opensearch_configuration.rst:86
msgid ""
"``admin_dn`` — Identifies the certificate authorized to run "
"administrative operations (e.g., ``securityadmin.sh``). Only requests "
"signed by a certificate matching this DN can modify the security index."
msgstr ""
"``admin_dn`` — Identifies the certificate authorized to run administrative "
"operations (e.g., ``securityadmin.sh``). Only requests signed by a "
"certificate matching this DN can modify the security index."

#: ../../getting_started/requirements/opensearch_configuration.rst:87
msgid ""
"``nodes_dn`` — Identifies certificates trusted for inter-node transport "
"communication. Nodes will reject transport connections from certificates "
"that don't match."
msgstr ""
"``nodes_dn`` — Identifies certificates trusted for inter-node transport "
"communication. Nodes will reject transport connections desde certificates "
"that don't match."

#: ../../getting_started/requirements/opensearch_configuration.rst:89
msgid "To extract the subject DN from an existing certificate:"
msgstr "To extract the subject DN desde an existente certificate:"

#: ../../getting_started/requirements/opensearch_configuration.rst:91
msgid "openssl x509 -in /path/to/cert.pem -noout -subject -nameopt RFC2253"
msgstr "openssl x509 -in /path/to/cert.pem -noout -subject -nameopt RFC2253"

#: ../../getting_started/requirements/opensearch_configuration.rst:95
msgid "Set the values in ``/etc/morpheus/morpheus.rb`` on each node:"
msgstr "Set the values in ``/etc/morpheus/morpheus.rb`` on cada nodo:"

#: ../../getting_started/requirements/opensearch_configuration.rst:97
msgid ""
"opensearch['admin_dn'] = 'CN=admin,OU=MyTeam,O=MyOrg'\n"
"opensearch['nodes_dn'] = 'CN=node,OU=MyTeam,O=MyOrg'"
msgstr ""
"opensearch['admin_dn'] = "
"'CN=admin,OU=MyTeam,O=MyOrg'\\nopensearch['nodes_dn'] = "
"'CN=node,OU=MyTeam,O=MyOrg'"

#: ../../getting_started/requirements/opensearch_configuration.rst:102
msgid ""
"If the admin and node certificates share the same DN (common when a "
"single wildcard or shared cert is used), both values can be set to the "
"same string. With the default auto-generated certificates, these are set "
"to ``O=Morpheus,OU=Ops,CN=<node_name>`` per node and do not need to be "
"configured manually."
msgstr ""
"If the admin y node certificates share the same DN (common when a single "
"wildcard o shared cert is used), both values puede ser set to the same "
"string. With the predeterminado auto-generated certificates, these are set "
"to ``O=Morpheus,OU=Ops,CN=<node_name>`` per node y do not necesita be "
"configurado manually."

#: ../../getting_started/requirements/opensearch_configuration.rst:105
msgid "Setting the Morpheus User Password"
msgstr "Setting the Morpheus User Password"

#: ../../getting_started/requirements/opensearch_configuration.rst:107
msgid ""
"When ``secure_mode`` is enabled, reconfigure creates an internal "
"OpenSearch user named ``morpheus`` that |morpheus| uses to authenticate "
"with OpenSearch. The password for this user is auto-generated and stored "
"in ``/etc/morpheus/morpheus-secrets.json`` under the "
"``elasticsearch.morpheus_password`` key. No manual configuration is "
"needed in the default case."
msgstr ""
"When ``secure_mode`` está habilitado, reconfigure creates an interno "
"OpenSearch user named ``morpheus`` that |morpheus| uses to authenticate "
"con OpenSearch. The password for this user is auto-generated y stored in "
"``/etc/morpheus/morpheus-secrets.json`` under the "
"``elasticsearch.morpheus_password`` key. No manual configuration is needed "
"in the predeterminado case."

#: ../../getting_started/requirements/opensearch_configuration.rst:109
msgid ""
"To set a custom password, add it to ``/etc/morpheus/morpheus.rb`` on each"
" node:"
msgstr ""
"To set a personalizado password, add it to ``/etc/morpheus/morpheus.rb`` "
"on cada nodo:"

#: ../../getting_started/requirements/opensearch_configuration.rst:111
msgid "opensearch['morpheus_password'] = 'my-custom-password'"
msgstr "opensearch['morpheus_password'] = 'my-custom-password'"

#: ../../getting_started/requirements/opensearch_configuration.rst:116
msgid "Encrypting the Password"
msgstr "Encrypting the Password"

#: ../../getting_started/requirements/opensearch_configuration.rst:118
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Passwords in ``morpheus.rb`` can be stored in encrypted form using the "
"``ENC{...}`` wrapper. During reconfigure, the recipe detects the ``ENC`` "
"prefix and decrypts the value automatically. Plaintext values are used "
"as-is."
msgstr ""
"Passwords in ``morpheus.rb`` puede ser stored in encrypted form using the "
"``ENC{...}`` wrapper. During reconfigure, the recipe detects the ``ENC`` "
"prefix y decrypts the value automatically. Plaintext values are used "
"as-is."

#: ../../getting_started/requirements/opensearch_configuration.rst:120
msgid "To generate an encrypted string:"
msgstr "To generate an encrypted string:"

#: ../../getting_started/requirements/opensearch_configuration.rst:122
msgid "morpheus-ctl get-crypto-string string 'my-custom-password'"
msgstr "morpheus-ctl get-crypto-string string 'my-custom-password'"

#: ../../getting_started/requirements/opensearch_configuration.rst:126
msgid "This outputs an encrypted value that can be used in ``morpheus.rb``:"
msgstr "This outputs an encrypted value that puede ser used in ``morpheus.rb``:"

#: ../../getting_started/requirements/opensearch_configuration.rst:128
#, python-brace-format
msgid "opensearch['morpheus_password'] = 'ENC{aBcDeFgHiJkLmNoPqRsTuVwXyZ...}'"
msgstr "opensearch['morpheus_password'] = 'ENC{aBcDeFgHiJkLmNoPqRsTuVwXyZ...}'"

#: ../../getting_started/requirements/opensearch_configuration.rst:132
msgid ""
"The encryption uses the appliance's ``encryption_key_suffix`` (from "
"``/etc/morpheus/morpheus-secrets.json``), so the encrypted value is "
"specific to that appliance. All nodes in the cluster share the same "
"secrets file contents, so the same encrypted string works on all nodes."
msgstr ""
"The encryption uses the appliance's ``encryption_key_suffix`` (from "
"``/etc/morpheus/morpheus-secrets.json``), so the encrypted value is "
"specific to that appliance. All nodes en la cluster share the same secrets "
"file contents, so the same encrypted string works on all nodes."

#: ../../getting_started/requirements/opensearch_configuration.rst:134
msgid ""
"Any password setting in ``morpheus.rb`` supports this format (under "
"either the ``opensearch[...]`` or ``elasticsearch[...]`` namespace), "
"including ``morpheus_password`` and ``auth_password``. As with other "
"settings, ``opensearch[...]`` takes precedence over "
"``elasticsearch[...]`` if both are set."
msgstr ""
"Any password setting in ``morpheus.rb`` supports this format (under either "
"the ``opensearch[...]`` o ``elasticsearch[...]`` namespace), including "
"``morpheus_password`` y ``auth_password``. As con other settings, "
"``opensearch[...]`` takes precedence over ``elasticsearch[...]`` if both "
"are set."

